WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.059 --> 00:00:17.180
What's goin on mah well read ballas? This
week sh*t gettin' absurdly cray with Hitchhikers

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:21.600
Guide to the Galaxy by Douglas Adams. Don't
panic, tho.

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:29.780
Normal British dude Arthur Dent got turnt
waaaayy up last night, and it'a all cuz deez

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:35.320
government haters bout bust up his crib to
make way fo' some lame-ass road. Pssh.

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:40.940
Just when Arthur gettin' all in this dude's grill,
his boy Ford Prefect roll by and be like "'Ey

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:46.519
don't sweat it, bruh. Da world bout to end."
"Wait...WHAT?" "Yeah man, some Vogons bout

00:00:46.519 --> 00:00:51.479
to blow this whole joint down to make some
kinda space road. Oh, yeah, and I'm an alien.

00:00:51.479 --> 00:00:57.070
S'all good." Jus' like he say- da Vogons
show up and BOOM. But Ford ain't trippin,

00:00:57.070 --> 00:01:00.519
cuz he jus' hitched him and Arthur a ride
on the Vogon spaceship.

00:01:00.519 --> 00:01:06.600
Arthur, tho- that boy buggin! To calm his ass
down, Ford like "fool shut up and read dis sh*t:

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:10.700
The Hitchiker's Guide to the Galaxy.
It'll teach you bout everything... no, fo'

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:15.900
real- everything." Arthur crack open what's
basically Wikipedia for da whole universe

00:01:15.909 --> 00:01:20.939
and start readin' bout Vogons. Arthur sees
da worst thing dat can happen when you rollin

00:01:20.939 --> 00:01:25.429
with Vogons is if they try to spit some of
their poetry yo' way. Apparently their flow

00:01:25.429 --> 00:01:29.899
is so lame, it can kill you! Plus they're
real assholes.

00:01:29.899 --> 00:01:34.579
So when the top dawg Volgon Jeltz found out
dat Arthur and Ford are bummin' a ride on

00:01:34.579 --> 00:01:39.140
his space hooptie, he lays down some ill rhymes
and gives em the boot.

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:44.710
Lucky fo' them, Ford's cousin Zaphod Beeblebrox
and his crew Trillian and Marvin just boosted

00:01:44.710 --> 00:01:50.109
a serious G-wagon called "The Heart of Gold."
And since they passin' by, da ship scoops

00:01:50.109 --> 00:01:53.090
em up befo' they suffocate and freeze they
asses off.

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:58.469
Turns out Zaphod is the president of the Galaxy
who actually partied with Arthur one time

00:01:58.469 --> 00:02:00.380
back on Earth. Small universe.

00:02:00.380 --> 00:02:05.600
Eventually they land on the planet Magrathea,
which used to be a swag spot fo' rich people

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:10.910
back in the day. After some whacked-out stuff
go down with a giant whale, they meet up with

00:02:10.910 --> 00:02:16.250
an old geezer named Slartibartfast. This dude
take em down to the core of da planet where

00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:18.819
they learn a buncha crazy-ass history.

00:02:18.820 --> 00:02:23.220
Apparently, some swole ass super computer
named DEEP THOUGHT pumped out da answer to

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:29.400
life, da universe, everything millions of years
ago- and it's da number 42. No' fo' real-

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:31.800
that's the answer to life. 42!

00:02:31.810 --> 00:02:36.200
Prollem is- the computer didn't know what
da hell da question was. So to figger that

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:40.750
out, the freakin MICE dat built it needed
a bigger, badder one: and that's where the

00:02:40.750 --> 00:02:46.470
Earth comes in. It was a 10 million year old
organic computer calculating dat very question,

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:52.329
and got blown to shit minutes before it was
bout to get da job done. Nice. Oh, and one

00:02:52.329 --> 00:02:56.500
more thing- these same mice used to be Trillian's
pets from Earth.

00:02:56.500 --> 00:03:01.250
Anyway, the mice runnin the show peep game
at Arthur the Earthman and start wonderin'

00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:07.329
if everything really lost: I mean if this dude's
brain came from Earth maybe da Ultimate Question

00:03:07.329 --> 00:03:12.560
is up in his dome!" Arthur like " Oh Hell
no. Y’all ain't even THINKIN bout touchin

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:16.780
dis brain." Dem mice don't play though, and
right as his mind bout to get fucked, Arthur

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:19.420
and his homies bust ass outta there.

00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:25.060
With the po-po still tailin Zaphod fo' boostin
dat clean-ass ride, they all decide- "man

00:03:25.060 --> 00:03:30.860
fuck it. Let's get some grub, yo" and high-tail
it to the Restaurant at the End of the Universe.

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:39.620
Man readin' this book is like watchin absurdist
stand up comedy, cuz that boy Douglas Addams

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:44.719
got MAD jokes. Just about erry single one
of em pointin' to da idea that ERRYTHING-

00:03:44.719 --> 00:03:51.370
da world, da solar system, da universe, ALL
OF IT- is completely RIDONKULOUS. Da stuff

00:03:51.370 --> 00:03:54.390
we think is big and meaningful ain't really
shit.

00:03:54.390 --> 00:04:00.799
"Far out in the uncharted backwaters lies
a small unregarded yellow sun. Orbiting this

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:07.320
is an utterly insignificant little blue-green
planet", whose life forms are "amazingly primitive"

00:04:07.540 --> 00:04:12.420
It ain't just da universe dat's whack- da
things livin' inside are pretty cray cray too.

00:04:12.430 --> 00:04:17.130
I mean errybody's got their priorities way
outta line. Like when da brains behind da

00:04:17.130 --> 00:04:22.250
Heart of Gold whip bout to meet Big Prez Beeblebrox
"There was a mood of immense excitement thrilling

00:04:22.250 --> 00:04:27.330
through all of them. Together and between
them they had gone to and beyond the furthest

00:04:27.330 --> 00:04:33.259
limits of physical laws, restructured the
fundamental fabric of matter, strained, twisted

00:04:33.259 --> 00:04:39.789
and broken the laws of possibility and impossibility,
but still the greatest excitement of all seemed

00:04:39.789 --> 00:04:43.360
to be to meet a man with an orange sash around
his neck. (39-40)

00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:48.960
Da Universe bein all random and goofy is actually
one part of a bigger theme of da book: thangs

00:04:48.970 --> 00:04:53.380
ain't always what they seem. Jus' when you
think you know what's comin', Adams messes

00:04:53.380 --> 00:04:57.700
with yo head and and make it totally different
from what you was expectin'. You know how

00:04:57.700 --> 00:05:01.960
errybody always sayin the world is so jacked
up cuz peeps don't know how to communicate

00:05:01.970 --> 00:05:07.220
with each other? Adams flips that shit right
on its head with da Babel fish. By stickin

00:05:07.220 --> 00:05:11.960
this nasty thang in yo ear, you can understand
every language in the universe. So if everybody

00:05:11.960 --> 00:05:16.710
can conversate with each other, errything's
all good, right? Wrong!

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:21.819
"Meanwhile, the poor Babel fish, by effectively
removing all barriers to communication between

00:05:21.819 --> 00:05:27.530
different races and cultures, has caused more
and bloodier wars than anything else in the

00:05:27.530 --> 00:05:29.099
history of creation." (60)

00:05:29.099 --> 00:05:34.530
Yeah- da universe is a crazy ass place where
coincidence, divine intervention, and science

00:05:34.530 --> 00:05:39.270
all look mo' alike then you might think. But
if you gonna take one thing away from this

00:05:39.270 --> 00:05:44.520
book it's this:
JUST CHILL. At da end of the day, it ain't

00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:50.669
worth tryna figger out all da who's and why's and how's.
Just look at how this conversation with Arthur

00:05:50.669 --> 00:05:51.849
and Salrtibartfast go:

00:05:51.849 --> 00:05:56.610
Arthur: "'All through my life I've had this
strange unaccountable feeling that something

00:05:56.610 --> 00:06:01.710
was going on in this world, something big,
even sinister, and no one would tell me what

00:06:01.710 --> 00:06:08.000
it was.' 'No,' said Slartibartfast, 'that's
just perfectly normal paranoia. Everyone in

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:13.700
the Universe has that.' 'Everyone?' said Arthur.
'Well, if everyone has that perhaps it means

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:19.720
something! Perhaps somewhere outside the Universe
we know’ 'Maybe. Who cares?' said Slartibartfast

00:06:19.729 --> 00:06:24.340
before Arthur got too excited. 'Perhaps I'm
old and tired,' he continued, 'but I always

00:06:24.340 --> 00:06:29.120
think that the chances of finding out what
really is going on are so absurdly remote

00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:34.040
that the only thing to do is to say hang the
sense of it and just keep yourself occupied."

00:06:34.280 --> 00:06:39.060
Best thing you can do is just sit back and
let crazy do what crazy gonna do.

